# ==============================================================================
# GMS Enterprise Vulnerability Exception & Suppression Registry (.trivyignore)
# ==============================================================================
# Governance Policy:
#   Every ignored CVE must have:
#     - Vulnerability ID (CVE-*)
#     - Affected Component / Base Package
#     - Business Impact & Threat Assessment
#     - Technical Mitigation & Non-Exploitability Justification
#     - Responsible Security Owner
#     - Expiry / Review Date (Mandatory 90-day maximum lifecycle)
#     - Upstream Target Fix Version
# ==============================================================================

# 1. CVE-2026-13149
# Component: node:22-alpine / internal libuv threadpool timing jitter
# Severity: HIGH (Base Score 7.1)
# Justification: DoS via algorithmic timing attack in libuv worker queue. Non-exploitable in GMS container runtime because network calls and DB queries use bounded threadpools and async I/O; no user-controllable CPU thread allocation is exposed.
# Owner: security-infrastructure-team@gms.local
# Expiry: 2026-11-30
# Upstream Fix: node:22.14.0-alpine (Pending release from upstream Alpine security team)
CVE-2026-13149

# 2. CVE-2026-14257
# Component: node:22-alpine / global npm bundled tar parser (pre-installed CLI tool)
# Severity: HIGH (Base Score 7.5)
# Justification: Arbitrary file overwrite if untrusted .tar archive is extracted via npm CLI. Non-exploitable because GMS production container runs in least-privilege mode (USER node), filesystem is read-only except /app/uploads, and npm CLI is not executed at runtime in production.
# Owner: security-infrastructure-team@gms.local
# Expiry: 2026-11-30
# Upstream Fix: npm v11.3.0
CVE-2026-14257

# 3. CVE-2026-69152
# Component: node:22-alpine / corepack bundled package manager stub
# Severity: MEDIUM/HIGH (Base Score 6.8)
# Justification: Remote code execution if corepack attempts to download untrusted yarn/pnpm binaries. Non-exploitable because corepack is disabled and network egress is isolated in production db-net/proxy-net.
# Owner: security-infrastructure-team@gms.local
# Expiry: 2026-11-30
# Upstream Fix: node:22.14.0-alpine
CVE-2026-69152

# 4. CVE-2026-40345
# Component: nginx:1.27.4-alpine / brotli compression buffer boundary edge case
# Severity: MEDIUM (Base Score 5.9)
# Justification: Memory leak on malformed brotli request bodies. Non-exploitable because brotli request decompression is disabled in deploy/nginx/nginx.conf; only gzip response compression is enabled.
# Owner: security-infrastructure-team@gms.local
# Expiry: 2026-11-30
# Upstream Fix: nginx:1.27.5-alpine
CVE-2026-40345

# 5. CVE-2026-69192
# Component: alpine:3.21 / busybox wget TLS host validation edge case
# Severity: MEDIUM (Base Score 6.1)
# Justification: TLS SNI mismatch in busybox wget CLI. Non-exploitable in GMS because wget is only used for local Docker healthcheck probing (http://127.0.0.1:80/health), not external network requests.
# Owner: security-infrastructure-team@gms.local
# Expiry: 2026-11-30
# Upstream Fix: busybox 1.37.1-r1
CVE-2026-69192

# 6. CVE-2026-33671
# Component: alpine:3.21 / zlib memory allocation on decompression bomb
# Severity: MEDIUM (Base Score 5.5)
# Justification: Resource exhaustion if decompressing untrusted gzip stream > 2GB. Non-exploitable because Nginx client_max_body_size is enforced at 10M across all ingress gateways.
# Owner: security-infrastructure-team@gms.local
# Expiry: 2026-11-30
# Upstream Fix: zlib 1.3.2-r0
CVE-2026-33671

# 7. CVE-2026-48815
# Component: node:22-alpine / v8 regex backtracking engine
# Severity: MEDIUM (Base Score 5.3)
# Justification: ReDoS on crafted regex input. Non-exploitable because all user inputs in GMS are validated with class-validator strict schemas and bounded length before reaching regex matchers.
# Owner: security-infrastructure-team@gms.local
# Expiry: 2026-11-30
# Upstream Fix: node:22.14.0-alpine
CVE-2026-48815

# 8. CVE-2026-59873
# Component: postgres:15.12-alpine / libcrypto3 TLS session resumption
# Severity: LOW/MEDIUM (Base Score 4.8)
# Justification: TLS session ticket reuse flaw. Non-exploitable because PostgreSQL port 5432 is not exposed to host network and communicates exclusively over internal Docker bridge network without external TLS listeners.
# Owner: security-infrastructure-team@gms.local
# Expiry: 2026-11-30
# Upstream Fix: openssl 3.3.3-r0
CVE-2026-59873

# 9. CVE-2026-59874
# Component: postgres:15.12-alpine / musl libc dynamic linker timing
# Severity: LOW (Base Score 3.7)
# Justification: Local user privilege escalation via dlsym timing side-channel. Non-exploitable because container runs under dedicated postgres UID with all Linux capabilities dropped (cap_drop: ALL) and no-new-privileges: true.
# Owner: security-infrastructure-team@gms.local
# Expiry: 2026-11-30
# Upstream Fix: musl 1.2.5-r2
CVE-2026-59874
